WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.825
Five stones hold jumps of 2, 3, 1, 1 and 4.

00:04.825 --> 00:07.294
Can you reach the end?

00:07.294 --> 00:14.700
Trying every route means following the same jumps again and again.

00:15.000 --> 00:18.340
Forget the route.

00:18.340 --> 00:31.700
Track one number instead: the farthest stone you could reach so far.

00:32.000 --> 00:38.531
Stone 1 jumps 3, stretching the reach to 4, the end.

00:38.531 --> 00:47.700
Now try 3, 2, 1, 0, 4: the reach stalls at 3, so stone 4 is out of reach.

00:48.000 --> 00:54.354
One scan, O(n) time: a stone past the reach means you’re stuck.

00:54.354 --> 00:59.700
That’s greedy: the best move now, never looking back.
